        en: '① Three project pages were rewritten so the facts carry the text. Every fact comes from the author own account of 2026-09-23; nothing that is not on the site or in that account was invented.\n② 6U104HP: the overview now states that a multifunction strip was designed above and below the module rows, describes the supply as the author own high-power low-ripple design, and presents the VESA holes as making the case equally at home playing out or in the studio, with a robot arm on the side of the Babel stack so that five cases, 3120HP of modules, can run together; the weight-reduction result now reads as the third version weighing 3.5kg fully loaded in most configurations. The exhibition record moved from restating the metadata dates to four passages of what happened on the floor: Music China 2024, where more than seventy oscillators sounded at once and someone asked how this differs from software and Tamix invited the pair to Modular Commune; Modular Commune 2024, where a clone of Mutable Elements was traded for a Tele Blender special edition and prototype cases were lent out across the hall; and the two 2025 shows, with the four-case Babel, conversations with developers from Behringer and Holocene, and module trades with Befaco and Instruō. The sales line gained about ten cases sold, a note that selling a product like this in China is difficult because it is too niche, too specialised and too large, and the overseas enquiries that have not worked out because of cost, paperwork and after-sales distance. The date and venue lines stay at the end, since the metadata block has no venue field.\n③ THE INDUCTION MIXER: the disembodiment paragraph is gone, the proposition is attributed to Christina Kubisch instead of reading as the author own, two passages of playing experience were added, and the two-states paragraph lost its exhibition-label vocabulary. The inspiration section was rebuilt around a real chain of attribution: the electromagnetic strand from Kubisch, the instrument strand from the work and writing of Cathy Van Eck and others, closing on the author own understanding of an instrument as a bridge between bodily action, inner hearing and the sound that comes out.\n④ riverrun: the review-voice paragraph and the closing aphorism were removed, the mechanism facts put in their place, and the author own sentence about hearing more while understanding less made the core line.\n⑤ The display name of the command-line tool in three documents was unified as the copy style ruler, in section 4 of AGENTS.md, section 9 of STYLEGUIDE.md and sections 12.4 and 16 of the engineering notes.\n⑥ Measured: the Chinese subset moves from 1,470 to 1,485 characters and the regular face from 277,464 to 280,428 bytes, with the font URL and the base.css number updated by the script to v18; both generators report no drift under check mode, verify.mjs passes all 653 assertions, and coverage.mjs reports an empty difference set.\n⑦ Rejected: sweeping every dash on the site into a colon, which would produce Chinese that does not sound like the author, leaving the remaining dashes for a later pass; naming the two friends, which the author ruled out; and writing the unclear sentence about small modules sold at a show.'
